      "page": "details",
      "excerpt": "InnoEnergy - Industrialising clean tech innovation Skip To Main Content Portfolio Ecosystem For Startups For Investors For Industry For Students Skills Institute About us Transitioning global energy Transforming every industry Contact us Head in the clouds. Feet on the ground. InnoEnergy is industrialising clean tech innovation to enable and grow a global net-zero economy We invest in early-stage companies and the current and future workforce, building resilient clean tech value chains that drive sustainable economic growth. Through the collective power of our ecosystem – with partners spanning industry, finance, public policy, and academia – we scale the energy transition at speed. We have been at the forefront of the clean energy transition since being initiated in 2010 by the European Institute of Innovation and Technology (EIT). Learn more about who we are 540 + Companies supported since 2010 160 + Active portfolio companies 2 .3 Gt Portfolio accumulated CO2e reduction potential by 2030 € 35 B+ Investment raised by portfolio companies through 2025 100 K+ Upskilled workers by end of 2024 2000 + Masters+ graduates We take a holistic approach to industrialising clean tech Invest in and de-risk early-stage startups Build new industrial champions Lead strategic industrial value chains Deliver upskilled talent for clean tech industries Prepare Masters graduates to lead the"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-a06cccb877",
      "url": "https://innoenergy.com/news-resources/accelerate-skellefteaa-2021-programme-opens-for-applications-for-clean-energy-startups-in-northern-sweden/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "Accelerate Skellefteå 2021 programme opens for applications for clean energy startups in Northern Sweden Skip To Main Content Portfolio Ecosystem For Startups For Investors For Industry For Students Skills Institute About us Jun 18, 2021 Accelerate Skellefteå 2021 programme opens for applications for clean energy startups in Northern Sweden Skellefteå, Sweden, is leading the green transformation in a region set to invest more than 70 billion Euros over the next 10 years and which has recently become a focal point for innovation in electrification and energy technology. To further propel the innovation process, the accelerator programme Accelerate Skellefteå is now issuing its second call to attract startups in clean energy technology to thrive and develop in a Scandinavian hotspot of energy, innovation, and growth. A growth opportunity for sustainable energy entrepreneurs Accelerate Skellefteå is a five-month long accelerator programme which aims to give startups with ideas in energy storage, mobility, and electrification the opportunity to further develop their concepts together with world-leading companies in Skellefteå, while also contributing to the momentum of innovation in existing industries. The initiative is operated jointly by EIT InnoEnergy, Skellefteå Kraft and Skellefteå Science City and this year also reinforced by the high-tech metals company Boliden and global"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-a1fdd598c1",
      "url": "https://innoenergy.com/news-resources/applications-for-the-second-edition-of-the-hello-cleantech-programme-for-cleantech-innovators-are-open/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "Applications for the second edition of the Hello CleanTech programme for cleantech innovators are open Skip To Main Content Portfolio Ecosystem For Startups For Investors For Industry For Students Skills Institute About us Nov 1, 2023 Applications for the second edition of the Hello CleanTech programme for cleantech innovators are open Start-ups, entrepreneurs, innovators and researchers who develop impactful tech solutions, accelerate the cleantech sector and make a real impact on the world’s energy industry can already apply for the Hello CleanTech 2.0 programme organised by EIT InnoEnergy alongside industry partners. In the first edition of the programme, over 250 applications were submitted, and 36 companies established cooperation with experienced market leaders, receiving business, technological and fundraising support. Hello CleanTech 2.0 The goal of the Hello CleanTech 2.0 programme is to create a platform that will enable start-ups, innovators and researchers to reach international corporations and establish potential cooperation. Among programme partners are: EIT InnoEnergy, Antler, Ciech Group, Commercialization Reactor, E44 ventures, EDP Renewables, Enea Innowacje, Enerco, Green Brother, Helve, Impact Prosper, South Poland Cleantech Cluster, World Fund, Cobin Angels, TDJ, Doral, Inci, Neurone, Boryszew, Sunly Startup, CofounderZone, Sabanci ARF, Warsaw Equity"
    },
