      "url": "https://innoenergy.com/news-resources/open-call-for-eit-innoenergy-hub-applications/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "Open call for EIT InnoEnergy Hub applications Skip To Main Content Portfolio Ecosystem For Startups For Investors For Industry For Students Skills Institute About us Jul 7, 2020 Open call for EIT InnoEnergy Hub applications EIT InnoEnergy Hubs are local offices operated by ambitious partners, who are looking to build their local position, strengthen their business model and become a leading actor in the local ecosystem by playing a role in our European Network. We are currently looking for partners to operate InnoEnergy Hubs supported by the EIT InnoEnergy Power Alliance platform in the following countries: Czechia, Greece, Lithuania, Estonia and Croatia. EIT InnoEnergy HUB’s scope Identify, develop, and support promising ideas, startups and entrepreneurs. Provide access to EIT InnoEnergy services Host and promote EIT InnoEnergy events (via the network of partners). Perform innovation capacity building services, pre-acceleration programmes. Actively promote the EIT InnoEnergy Business Model and actively participate in the local ecosystem Perform local business development services and support sales channels for EIT InnoEnergy portfolio. I Stage – application and shortlist (max 100 p) You apply by sending your application and we will select the best candidates according to the Evaluation ScoreBoard.The ones that pass over the minimum threshold will qualify for Stage II. Maximum"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-page-2421f3e5b8",
      "url": "https://innoenergy.com/news-resources/webinar-battery-storage-applications/",
      "page": "application",
      "excerpt": "Webinar | Battery Storage Applications Skip To Main Content Portfolio Ecosystem For Startups For Investors For Industry For Students Skills Institute About us Feb 11, 2020 Webinar | Battery Storage Applications Battery storage is set to completely disrupt the energy space and shape the future of the sector for the foreseeable future. The EU estimates that in Europe alone, the battery storage market will be worth €250 billion by 2025. Exploiting the opportunities to come and securing competitive edge in the longer-term starts with building the understanding of the different battery storage applications. The importance of batteries Energy and battery storage is at the heart of strategy for the European energy transition and is a rapidly expanding market. Battery storage can be deployed at different levels of the electricity system, providing a broad variety of values and allowing access to multiple revenue streams. Therefore, the battery storage industry is generating a vast interest and the number of investors looking to enter this market is continuously growing. Nonetheless, many are still having difficulties understanding how they could benefit from battery storage. In this free webinar, Johan Söderbom, Thematic Leader in Smart Grids and Energy Storage at EIT InnoEnergy will focus on providing you a comprehensive overview of the battery storage applications. Register"
    },
